        "image": ""
      }
    ],
    "correctAnswer": "A",
    "explanation": "Explanation: [Cr(CN)6]3- has Cr3+ (d3), which has 3 unpaired electrons (A-II). [Fe(H2O)6]2+ has Fe2+ (d6 high-spin), which has 4 unpaired electrons (B-IV). [Co(NH3)6]3+ has Co3+ (d6 low-spin), which has 0 unpaired electrons (C-I). [Ni(NH3)6]2+ has Ni2+ (d8), which has 2 unpaired electrons (D-III). Matching is A-II, B-IV, C-I, D-III, which is option A.",
